# ============================================
# CREDENTIAL MANAGEMENT NOTE
# ============================================
#
# This project uses config.json for credentials instead of .env
# This is the idiomatic pattern for PowerShell projects.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Copy config.json.template to config.json
#   2. Edit config.json with your credentials
#   3. config.json is gitignored and will not be committed
#
# ============================================
# REQUIRED CREDENTIALS (in config.json)
# ============================================
#
# FTP.Host         - Carbonite switcher IP address
# FTP.Port         - FTP port (default: 21)
# FTP.Username     - FTP username (default: user)
# FTP.Password     - FTP password (default: password)
#
# ============================================
# OPTIONAL CREDENTIALS (in config.json)
# ============================================
#
# Email.Username   - SMTP authentication username
# Email.Password   - SMTP authentication password (use App Password for Gmail)
#
# ============================================
# SECURITY
# ============================================
#
# - Never commit config.json to version control
# - Restrict file permissions on config.json
# - Change default ROSS passwords in production
# - Use App Passwords for Gmail/Office365
#
# See docs/reference/security.md for details
